  TNK:  {price_usd: 77.1,  consensus_pnav: 0.80, consensus_fwd_pe: 8.9}
  STNG: {price_usd: 76.4,  consensus_pnav: 0.71, consensus_fwd_pe: 13.0}
  TRMD: {price_usd: 29.5,  consensus_pnav: 0.86, consensus_fwd_pe: 9.9}
  HAFN: {price_usd: 7.6,   consensus_pnav: 0.92, consensus_fwd_pe: 9.5}
  CMBT: {price_usd: 16.4,  consensus_pnav: 0.85, consensus_fwd_pe: 10.2}
  GNK:  {price_usd: 25.1,  consensus_pnav: 0.92, consensus_fwd_pe: 13.7}
  SBLK: {price_usd: 28.6,  consensus_pnav: 0.89, consensus_fwd_pe: 7.2}
  LPG:  {price_usd: 44.4,  consensus_pnav: 0.96, consensus_fwd_pe: 12.2}
  FLNG: {price_usd: 31.0,  consensus_pnav: 1.43, consensus_fwd_pe: 14.9}
  BRUT: {price_kr: 60.0,   consensus_pnav: 0.86, consensus_fwd_pe: 22.6}   # NOK — FX at promote
  CAPT: {price_kr: 134.2,  consensus_pnav: 0.71, consensus_fwd_pe: 22.2}   # NOK — FX at promote
  BWLP: {price_kr: 206.6,  consensus_pnav: 1.13, consensus_fwd_pe: 11.6}   # NOK — FX at promote

approx_basis:            # Pareto publishes NO P/NAV — price + fwd P/E legs only, pnav stays APPROX-flagged
  ASC:  {price_usd: 17.0, consensus_fwd_pe: 15.5}
  NAT:  {price_usd: 6.4,  consensus_fwd_pe: 18.7}
  CCEC: {price_usd: 22.8, consensus_fwd_pe: 7.9}
  MPCC: {price_kr: 24.2,  consensus_fwd_pe: 8.1}    # NOK — FX at promote

absent_from_table:       # keep the FULL consensus-pair anchor at its CURRENT vintage.
  # NOT "just the price": the pipeline already values every name at the live
  # prices_daily close — what these five keep is the watchlist STATIC pair
  # (price + consensus_pnav + consensus_fwd_pe) as one older vintage. NEVER
  # move a watchlist price against a stale pnav (the TEN $44 lesson — and TEN
  # is in this bucket).
  - TEN
  - SB
  - CMDB
  - GSL
  # "2343" MOVED OUT 2026-08-13 -> issuer_sourced below. It is still absent from
  # Pareto's table (that is unchanged and always will be — no HK names), but its
  # anchor was never Pareto's: it is an ISSUER-COMPOSITE derivation, and the issuer
  # just republished the input. Keeping it in this bucket would have held a Dec-2025
  # value vintage that the 2026 Interim has already superseded.

issuer_sourced:            # ADDED 2026-08-13 — names whose consensus_pnav is derived
  # from an ISSUER-published fleet value, not a broker table. These rebase on the
  # issuer's OWN reporting calendar, not Pareto's daily, so they are a separate lane
  # with a separate as_of. Do not merge them into pareto_basis.
  "2343":
    nav_per_share_usd: 0.4297      # <- PROMOTE THIS, then compute pnav from it
    basis_as_of: 2026-06-30
    source: >
      HKEX doc 12275567_2026080601217 (2026 Interim Results, published 2026-08-06),
      Business Review: "As at 30 June 2026, the estimated market value of our owned
      fleet was about US$2,070.6 million, which was significantly above its net book
      value of US$1,557.0 million."
    derivation: >
      NAV = fleet 2,070.6 + cash 206.530 + working capital 85.838 - debt 49.309
      - lease liabilities 93.957 = US$2,219.7M / 5,165.247803M shares = $0.4297/sh.
      Balance-sheet legs are the LANDED 2026-Q2 sheet (inputs/balance_sheets/
      2343_2026-Q2.yaml, same filing), so fleet value and balance sheet share one
      2026-06-30 vintage — no cross-vintage mixing inside the anchor itself.
    supersedes: >
      The Dec-2025 basis: fleet 1,958.3 + VUC 39.6 + cash 270.6 + WC 26.4 - debt 136.5
      - leases 93.9 = US$2,064.5M / 5,165.2M = $0.3997/sh (AR2025 p.6, 31-Dec-2025).
      Fleet +5.7%, NAV/sh +7.5%. This lands where the old watchlist comment predicted
      ("the true current pnav runs LOWER, ~0.87-0.9") — a reproduction check, not a
      coincidence: the derivation was re-run from the issuer figures, not back-solved.
    double_count_check: >
      The Dec-2025 line carried a SEPARATE vessels-under-construction leg (+39.6). The
      Q2 sheet books newbuilds through newbuild_capex_commitments (344.5) under the
      §9.6 convention, so VUC is NOT added again here. Adding it would have silently
      inflated NAV/sh by ~$0.008. Verify this stays true if the sheet convention changes.
    known_gap: >
      The Interim gives a SINGLE AGGREGATE fleet value. The AR2025 published a PER-CLASS
      composite (Handysize/Supramax/Ultramax). The derivation only ever consumed the
      total, so nothing breaks — but a future per-class refinement cannot be sourced
      from this document. Next per-class disclosure: AR2026 (~Mar-2027).
    pnav_rule: >
      DO NOT hardcode a pnav. consensus_pnav = promoted_price / 0.4297, computed at
      promote from whatever price leg is promoted in the SAME commit. At the current
      stale $0.390 (2026-07-14 close) that is 0.91 (was 0.98). Deriving it this way
      makes a price/pnav vintage skew structurally impossible for this name — the
      TEN $44 lesson, enforced by construction rather than by discipline.
    flags_unchanged: APPROX stays (no broker coverage); /reconcile keeps downweighting.

promote_checklist:       # (WORKFLOWS §Consensus-pair recapture steps 4-5 — the
  # off-cycle sitting still owes ALL of it; reviewer catch 2026-08-09)
  - "One commit rebasing watchlist.yaml from this draft (FX rule: price leg only, daily-date FX; delete this draft in the same commit)"
  - "Gate loop: pytest -> /reconcile --all -> drift gate. k_broker WILL move on its second difference (that is the rebase's purpose) -> annotate movers, then ratify"
  - "Drafted ratify cause: 'watchlist consensus-pair rebase to the 2026-08-07 Pareto daily (one vintage, 20 names; APPROX flags kept on NAT/ASC/CCEC/MPCC; retires the 8/09 k-vintage-skew — re-examine TXN_PURE_PLAY_K_BAND and the REFRESH_VINTAGE_SKEW allowance at this ratify, with a scoped APPROX-name replacement for the retired allowance)'"
  - "Record the sitting in decisions/ (this file's header is the transcription record); re-arm all_sectors_consensus_pair_recapture from due 2026-10-02 to promote-date + 3 months"
  - "Band flips from the price move: isolate-commit discipline, individual eyeballs"
  - "2343 (issuer_sourced lane): promote nav_per_share_usd 0.4297 and COMPUTE consensus_pnav = promoted_price / 0.4297 in the same commit — never paste a pnav. Expect ~0.98 -> ~0.91 at an unchanged price. Its consensus_fwd_pe (13.0, stockanalysis 2026-07-14) is a SEPARATE aggregator vintage untouched by the Interim — leave it, and say so in the commit rather than letting it look refreshed"
  - "2343 re-arm: the next issuer-composite refresh is AR2026 (~Mar-2027, per-class values return there). The 2026 Interim trigger is now SPENT — retire the 'Re-derive at the 2026 Interim' line from the watchlist comment at promote so a future reader does not chase a fired trigger"

